.TH SCOUT.PY 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
scout.py \- the @scout lane: poll advisory feeds for CVE IDs the fleet has not seen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scout.py
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
.RB [ \-\-feeds
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-print\-new ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-db ]
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent scout.py
.I options
.br
.B python3 $FLEET_CODE/lanes/scout.py
.I options
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scout.py
reads every RSS 2.0 or Atom feed in the feed list, pulls CVE IDs out of each
entry's title, description, summary and content, and reports the ones that
are neither in the findings table nor already recorded by an earlier scout
run. It is run by
.B cti\-agent\-scout.timer
every four hours, at 00:15, 04:15, 08:15, 12:15, 16:15 and 20:15, with
.B \-\-days 3
and its output in
.IR /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/scout\-latest.json .
.PP
Entries older than the window are skipped; an entry whose date cannot be
parsed (RFC 822 or ISO 8601, from
.BR pubDate ,
.BR published ,
.B updated
or
.BR date )
is kept. A feed counts as failed when it cannot be fetched (30-second
timeout), returns an HTML page instead of XML (logged as
.BR "NOT A FEED" ,
usually a feed that has moved), is malformed XML, or contains no entries.
Failed feeds are named on standard error at the end of the run, because a
dead feed is a blind spot that otherwise looks like a quiet day.
.PP
Unless
.B \-\-no\-db
is given and
.I memory.db
exists, every CVE mentioned in the window, new or not, is recorded in the
.B scout_items
table with up to three of its sources (one row per CVE and feed; an existing
row is left alone). That record is what makes a CVE not new on the next run.
.PP
This lane finds candidates. It never decides exposure, does not run the
scanner, and sends no mail. Progress goes to standard error, prefixed
.BR [scout] .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-out " FILE"
Required. Where to write the JSON result:
.B new_cves
(sorted),
.B all_mentioned
(every CVE seen in the window),
.B detail
(feed, title, link and date for each new CVE), and the feed counts and
failed URLs. Missing directories are created.
.TP
.BI \-\-feeds " FILE"
The feed list: one URL per line; blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
in the first column are skipped.
Default:\~\fB$FLEET_FEEDS\fR, else \fI$FLEET_HOME/lanes/feeds.txt\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
Ignore entries published more than
.I N
days ago. An integer.
Default:\~\fB3\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-new
Also print the new CVEs on standard output, comma-separated on one line
(an empty line when there are none), ready for
.BR "enrich.py \-\-cves" .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-db
Do not open
.I memory.db
at all: every CVE mentioned counts as new, and nothing is recorded.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B scout.py
does not load
.I fleet.env
itself; the systemd unit does, and so does the
.BR cti\-agent (1)
wrapper on a hand run.
.TP
.B FLEET_FEEDS
Default for
.BR \-\-feeds .
.I fleet.env
section 3, PATHS; set to
.I /etc/cti\-agent/feeds.txt
by the unit and the wrapper.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
State directory; the database is
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/memory.db .
Default:\~\fI~/fleet\fR. Section 3.
.TP
.B FLEET_USER_AGENT
User-Agent sent to the feeds.
Default:\~\fB\%cti\-agent\-scout/1.0\fR.
Section 6, ENRICHMENT.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cti\-agent/feeds.txt
The feed list.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/scout\-latest.json
The timer's output.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/memory.db
Read for known CVEs
.RB ( findings
and
.B scout_items
tables) and written
.RB ( scout_items ).
Never created by this lane: when it is missing, every CVE is new and
nothing is recorded.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The result was written, even if every feed failed. Read
.B feeds_failed
in the output or the log to tell a quiet day from a blind one.
.TP
.B 1
The feed list does not exist; or the output could not be written (Python
traceback).
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments: no
.BR \-\-out ,
or a non-integer
.BR \-\-days .
.SH EXAMPLES
What the last sweep found, and which feeds failed:
.PP
.EX
sudo journalctl \-u cti\-agent\-scout \-\-since today
sudo python3 \-m json.tool /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/scout\-latest.json
.EE
.PP
A wider look that records nothing, printing every CVE mentioned:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent scout.py \-\-no\-db \-\-days 7 \-\-print\-new \e
  \-\-out /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/scout\-test.json
.EE
.PP
Test a candidate feed before adding it:
.PP
.EX
echo https://feeds.example.com/advisories.xml > /tmp/feeds.txt
python3 fleet\-kit/fleet/lanes/scout.py \-\-no\-db \e
  \-\-feeds /tmp/feeds.txt \-\-out /tmp/scout.json
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR enrich.py (1),
.BR fleet\-db (1),
.BR fleet\-board (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 9; fleet\-kit/README.md, "Troubleshooting" (dead feeds).
